  "rationale": "The representative error is a noun after “Tom and the”: the model favors nouns licensed by a preceding determiner but gives apples almost no mass in this coordinated opening. The batch also repeatedly uses “And so,” while the so root is extremely underweighted, and includes an adjective followed by day, which the day root does not specifically support. A sentence-ending period after now is another low-mass continuation. Add bounded contextual rules for these patterns, plus a reusable suffix rule for a coordinated determiner phrase followed by a noun and paragraph break. These rules raise likelihood for observed classes without making alternatives impossible. Counterexamples are possible: a different noun can follow “and the,” an adjective need not precede day, and other continuations after And or now can be valid; the additions therefore remain contextual rather than global.",
